# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the asbind20 test suite.
#
# Usage:
#   TSAN_OPTIONS="suppressions=$PWD/ci/tsan.supp" ctest --output-on-failure
#
# The suppressed reports come from the AngelScript dependency, not from
# asbind20 itself.
#
# asCScriptFunction::AddRef()/Release() (as_scriptfunction.cpp) contain a
# non-atomic write of the one-byte `gcFlag` member next to the atomic external
# reference count. Preparing/invoking the same script function from several
# threads at once (as MTStrFactoryTest* does) therefore makes those writes
# race. This is an upstream issue that still exists in AngelScript 2.40.0 WIP;
# the write is a plain store of `false`, but it is still undefined behaviour.
#
# Remove these entries once upstream AngelScript makes `gcFlag` atomic or
# removes the write.
race:asCScriptFunction::AddRef
race:asCScriptFunction::Release
